{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Hear, my son, the discipline</b> etc. <b>the Torah of your mother</b> — for the woman is wise, instructing her son in the straight path, like Bathsheba, who instructed Lemuel. And the word <i>el</i> is a term of persuasion, from the root of <i>ma'aneh</i> (answer), and from the same root <i>'el komo mot</i> [he answered him...]."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The final Hebrew phrase אלקום עמו אל מות is obscure; read here as אל קום עמו אל מות from Proverbs 26:19, but the segmentation and meaning remain uncertain; rendered hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:42.546972544Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}